    <!-- Instructions -->
    <sys:String x:Key="Instr_Welcome">Welcome to Anime Tracker!</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Instr_Subtitle">Your personal companion in the world of anime</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Instr_Intro">Keep a personal anime catalog, rate titles by 10 criteria and build your own top.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Instr_QuickStart_Title">Quick start</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Instr_Step1_Title">Add</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Instr_Step1_Text">Press “Add” on the Plan tab</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Instr_Step2_Title">Watch</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Instr_Step2_Text">Set the status to “Watching”</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Instr_Step3_Title">Rate</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Instr_Step3_Text">The “Watched” status opens rating</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Instr_Step4_Title">Share</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Instr_Step4_Text">Save your plan or top as an image</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Instr_Plan_Title">Plan tab</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Instr_Plan_1">➕ “Add” opens a form: title, genres, description, voice-over, seasons, movies, OVAs and ONAs.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Instr_Plan_2">🔄 Change the status right in the table: “Plan” → “Watching” → “Watched”. With the last status the anime moves to the Rating tab.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Instr_Plan_3">⭐ “Temp Rating” — rate the selected anime in advance or while watching. The scores carry over when you mark it “Watched”.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Instr_Plan_4">🎲 “Random” picks a random anime from your plan — you can narrow it down by genre.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Instr_Plan_5">✏️ “Edit” and “Delete” work with the selected row. Use the title search to find what you need.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Instr_Rating_Title">Rating tab</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Instr_Rating_1">🎯 Every season and movie is rated by 10 criteria: from story and characters to sound and finale. The “Criteria” button explains what each score means. OVAs and ONAs are only listed as part of a title (they show up in the plan, top and statistics) but are not rated.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Instr_Rating_2">🎵 Openings and endings are rated separately. Their number is detected automatically, but you can change it with ➖ and ➕.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Instr_Rating_3">⚖️ If two anime end up with the same score, the app will ask which one is better.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Instr_Rating_4">↩️ “Cancel Rating” returns the anime to your plan with the “Watching” status.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Instr_Top_Title">Top tab</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Instr_Top_1">🏆 Your personal ranking by final score, accurate to hundredths. The leaders are highlighted.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Instr_Top_2">🔁 “Re-evaluate” sends a title back to the Rating tab, “Edit” changes its info without losing scores, “Delete from Top” removes the entry.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Instr_Top_3">🔍 The title search works here too.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Instr_Share_Title">“Share” button</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Instr_Share_1">🖼 Available on the Plan and Top tabs: creates a beautiful image with the logo and the list from the current table (search is taken into account).</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Instr_Share_2">📚 If there are many anime, the list is automatically split into several images — nothing gets cut off.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Instr_Share_3">💾 The image uses your theme colors and the app language. You can save it as PNG or JPEG.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Instr_Stats_Title">Statistics tab</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Instr_Stats_1">📈 Summary: how many anime are watched, planned and currently being watched, plus total time and episode count.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Instr_Stats_2">🍩 Charts show your favorite genres, top 10, trends by year, the longest and shortest titles, and recommendations. The data comes from the Top tab.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Instr_Settings_Title">Settings tab</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Instr_Settings_1">🎨 Pick one of 9 themes and the interface language — Russian or English. Changes apply instantly.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Instr_Settings_2">🛟 Backups are created automatically when you save (at most once every 30 minutes). Up to 5 latest copies from the past week are kept; restore or delete them in “Manage backups”.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Instr_Settings_3">📤 Export and 📥 import move the animeData.json file — handy when switching to another computer.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Instr_Settings_4">⚠️ “Reset Data” permanently deletes your whole catalog. If unsure, export first.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Instr_Hotkeys_Title">Hotkeys</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Instr_Hotkeys_1">Jump straight to the search box on the Plan and Top tabs.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Instr_Footer">Enjoy watching! 🍿</sys:String>

    <!-- FAQ -->
    <sys:String x:Key="FAQ_Title">Frequently Asked Questions</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="FAQ_Q1">How to add anime?</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="FAQ_A1">Click the "Add" button on the "Plan" tab, fill in the required fields (marked with *), and click "Add". If you immediately select "Watched" status, the anime will move to the "Rating" tab.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="FAQ_Q2">Why are genres not displayed?</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="FAQ_A2">Make sure you have selected a main genre from the dropdown. Additional genres are optional.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="FAQ_Q3">What if two anime have the same score?</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="FAQ_A3">When adding to the top, a selection window will open where you decide which anime to rank higher. If conflicts remain, the system will prompt you to resolve them at startup.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="FAQ_Q4">How to restore data from a backup?</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="FAQ_A4">On the "Settings" tab, click "Manage backups", select the desired copy and click "Restore". You can also import a previously exported data file.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="FAQ_Q5">How to completely erase all data?</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="FAQ_A5">On the "Settings" tab, in the "Data Management" section, click the red "Reset Data" button. Confirm the action in the popup window (you need to wait 5 seconds). It is strongly recommended to create a backup before resetting.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="FAQ_Q6">Why does the "Top" tab lag slightly when first opened?</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="FAQ_A6">When you first switch to the "Top" tab, the app calculates statistics and finalizes score sorting. This is completely normal and takes only a fraction of a second. Subsequent openings will be instant.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="FAQ_Q7">How to rate anime if each season has a different number of openings/endings?</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="FAQ_A7">The system automatically determines the number of openings/endings based on season length (≤12 ep – 1, 13–24 ep – 2, 25–36 ep – 3, etc.). You can manually add or remove sliders using the «+» and «−» buttons next to each list. If the anime has a non‑standard amount (e.g., a different ending in every episode), we recommend calculating the average of all themes and entering it into a single slider.</sys:String>
